Subject: Number to string finds the shortest decimal of a double with at most 15 significant digits by exact double arithmetic

What this does
  - new `js_dtoa_short`: for 1e-6 <= |d| < 1e15, the smallest k (0..15) with R = round(|d| * 10^k) and R / 10^k == |d| gives the digits of R with the point k places from the right; when R has more than 15 digits, or no k works, it returns 0
  - `js_dtoa2` (radix 10, free format: Number.prototype.toString, String(x), concatenation) and JSON.stringify's double case try it before js_dtoa

Why we need it
  js_dtoa's multi-precision shortest search was 27% of stringify cycles on the app-traffic benchmark (prices, scores). json_app stringify only: -13.2% cycles, -8.7% instructions.

Soundness
  R and 10^k are exact doubles (R <= 2^53, k <= 15), so R / 10^k is rounded once and equality is exactly the round trip of the decimal R e-k. No decimal with fewer fraction digits round-trips (a smaller k was tried), and at most one decimal of 15 or fewer significant digits rounds to a given double (DBL_DIG), so it is the shortest and the nearest, which js_dtoa returns. 1e-6 <= |d| < 1e15 is inside the fixed-notation range of Number.prototype.toString. Differential, old engine vs new: 1,500,000 doubles (short decimals, random magnitudes over 30 decades, random bit patterns incl. NaN/denormals, sums like 0.1*n+0.2, the range boundaries 1e-6/1e15/1e21, -0) print the same through String, JSON.stringify and concatenation.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 149f5d5..da0cf80 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -23682,6 +23682,58 @@ static JSValue js_bigint_to_string(JSContext *ctx, JSValueConst val)
 
 /*---- floating point number to string conversions ----*/
 
+/* The shortest round-trip decimal of d in the fixed notation of Number.prototype.toString, when it has at most 15 significant digits
+   and 1e-6 <= |d| < 1e15; 0 (nothing written) otherwise. For the smallest k with R = round(|d| * 10^k) and R / 10^k == |d| (both
+   exact doubles, R <= 2^53 and k <= 15, so the division is rounded once and the test is the round trip), R/10^k is the answer: no
+   decimal with fewer fraction digits round-trips, and at most one decimal of 15 or fewer significant digits rounds to a given double,
+   so it is also the one nearest to d. */
+static int js_dtoa_short(char *buf, double d)
+{
+    static const double p10[16] = { 1e0, 1e1, 1e2, 1e3, 1e4, 1e5, 1e6, 1e7, 1e8, 1e9, 1e10, 1e11, 1e12, 1e13, 1e14, 1e15 };
+    double a = fabs(d), v;
+    uint64_t r;
+    char dig[24];
+    int k, nd, i, n = 0;
+
+    if (!(a >= 1e-6 && a < 1e15))
+        return 0;
+    for (k = 0; k <= 15; k++) {
+        v = a * p10[k];
+        if (v >= 9007199254740992.0)
+            return 0;
+        r = (uint64_t)(v + 0.5);
+        if ((double)r / p10[k] == a)
+            break;
+    }
+    if (k > 15 || r == 0)
+        return 0;
+    nd = 0;
+    while (r != 0) {
+        dig[nd++] = (char)('0' + r % 10);
+        r /= 10;
+    }
+    if (nd > 15)
+        return 0;
+    if (d < 0)
+        buf[n++] = '-';
+    if (nd <= k) {
+        buf[n++] = '0';
+        buf[n++] = '.';
+        for (i = 0; i < k - nd; i++)
+            buf[n++] = '0';
+        for (i = nd - 1; i >= 0; i--)
+            buf[n++] = dig[i];
+    } else {
+        for (i = nd - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
+            buf[n++] = dig[i];
+            if (i == k && k > 0)
+                buf[n++] = '.';
+        }
+    }
+    buf[n] = '\0';
+    return n;
+}
+
 static JSValue js_dtoa2(JSContext *ctx,
                         double d, int radix, int n_digits, int flags)
 {
@@ -23689,6 +23741,11 @@ static JSValue js_dtoa2(JSContext *ctx,
     int len, len_max;
     JSValue res;
     JSDTOATempMem dtoa_mem;
